-- title:
--   Upper-triangular δ with central norm class is a scalar coboundary
-- statement:
--   Let $L/F$ be a finite Galois extension of fields with $F$ infinite, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/F)$ be such that every $F$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ have vanishing lower-left entry, i.e. the underlying matrix satisfies $\delta_{1,0} = 0$, and let $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be either elliptic, in the sense that no element of $F$ is a root of the characteristic polynomial of the matrix of $\gamma$, or central, in the sense that this matrix is $c \cdot 1$ for some $c \in F$. Assume that the $\sigma$-twisted norm class of $\delta$ maps to the conjugacy class of $\gamma$: writing `SigmaConjClasses` for the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ by the relation $\delta_1 \sim \delta_2$ iff $\delta_2 = k^{-1}\delta_1\,\sigma(k)$ for some $k \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ ($\sigma$ acting entrywise), and `normClassMap` for the map induced on that quotient by sending $\delta$ to the conjugacy class in $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ of the chosen $F$-rational norm representative `normRep hgen δ`, the hypothesis is `normClassMap hgen (SigmaConjClasses.mk σ δ) = ConjClasses.mk γ`. The conclusion is that there exist $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $u \in L^{\times}$ with $\delta = (u \cdot 1)\,\bigl(h^{-1}\,\sigma(h)\bigr)$, where $\sigma(h)$ denotes the entrywise image of $h$ under $\sigma$.
--
--   This is the $\mathrm{GL}_2$ case of the standard fact, going back to Langlands' analysis of $\sigma$-conjugacy in base change, that an upper-triangular element whose twisted norm class is central is $\sigma$-conjugate to a scalar, the elliptic alternative in the hypothesis being vacuous for such $\delta$ since its norm has the $F$-rational eigenvalue $N_{L/F}(\delta_{0,0})$. It is used in the bound [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_encard_setOf_twistedKernelSummand_ne_zero_not_identityFamily_le`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_encard_setOf_twistedKernelSummand_ne_zero_not_identityFamily_le), where terms indexed by non-scalar $\sigma$-conjugacy classes must be discarded.
